MAT","name":"Matthew","slug":"matthew","live":true,"x":44,"y":629}],"portalColor":{"OT":"#8C93AD","NT":"#D8DCEB"},"groups":[{"label":"Creation","color":"#7FB77E"},{"label":"Noah","color":"#4EA8DE"},{"label":"Abraham","color":"#D9A441"},{"label":"Moses","color":"#C05746"},{"label":"David","color":"#B07CD4"},{"label":"New covenant","color":"#E4DFCE"},{"label":"Unassigned","color":"#5A6178"}],"relkinds":[{"key":"quoted-in","label":"Quoted in","color":"#E8C15A","strong":true},{"key":"fulfilled-in","label":"Fulfilled in","color":"#D9715C","strong":true},{"key":"parallels","label":"Parallels","color":"#6E9BD1","strong":false},{"key":"illustrates-doctrine","label":"Illustrates doctrine","color":"#9B8AD1","strong":false},{"key":"part-of-covenant","label":"Part of covenant","color":"#5FBFA0","strong":false}],"counts":{"topics":5,"portals":2,"edges":4,"relations":3,"outbound":3},"nodes":[{"id":"bt_book_jon","p":0,"x":56,"y":109,"s":-1,"g":6,"bk":"JON","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"Jonah: overview","d":"A narrative of the prophet Jonah son of Amittai, sent to Nineveh: he flees, is caught in a storm and swallowed by a great fish, then preaches, Nineveh repents, and the LORD answers Jonah's anger with a question about pity for the city.","q":"Can {{name}} retell the book of Jonah in a few sentences and say how it ends?","ev":["Retell the four chapters in order","Say what question the book ends on (4:11)"],"pp":[[31,1,1,17],[31,2,1,10],[31,3,1,10],[31,4,1,11]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_jon_flees_storm","p":0,"x":56,"y":239,"s":0,"g":6,"bk":"JON","ty":"STORY","t":"Jonah flees and the storm","d":"Told to go to Nineveh, Jonah goes the other way toward Tarshish; the LORD sends a great storm, the sailors cast lots and Jonah is thrown into the sea, whereupon the sea calms and the men fear the LORD.","q":"Can {{name}} retell why the storm came in Jonah 1 and how it stopped?","ev":["Say what the LORD told Jonah to do and what he did","Tell what Jonah said about himself in 1:9 and 1:12","Say how the sailors responded in 1:14-16"],"pp":[[31,1,1,16]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_jon_fish_prayer","p":0,"x":56,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"JON","ty":"STORY","t":"Jonah in the fish","d":"The LORD prepares a great fish that swallows Jonah for three days and three nights; from its belly Jonah prays, remembers the LORD and declares that salvation is of the LORD, and the fish casts him on dry land.","q":"Can {{name}} tell what happened to Jonah after he was thrown into the sea and what he prayed?","ev":["Tell how long Jonah was in the fish","Describe what Jonah says in his prayer (2:2, 2:9)"],"pp":[[31,1,17,17],[31,2,1,10]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_jon_nineveh_repents","p":0,"x":56,"y":499,"s":2,"g":6,"bk":"JON","ty":"STORY","t":"Nineveh believes and God spares","d":"The word comes to Jonah a second time; he cries that Nineveh will be overthrown in forty days, the people and their king fast, wear sackcloth and turn from their evil way, and God sees their works and does not do the harm he said.","q":"Can {{name}} retell how Nineveh responded to Jonah's preaching and what God did?","ev":["Retell Jonah's message and the response of Nineveh","Say what God did in 3:10"],"pp":[[31,3,1,10]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_jon_anger_and_gourd","p":0,"x":244,"y":499,"s":2,"g":6,"bk":"JON","ty":"STORY","t":"Jonah's anger and the gourd","d":"Jonah is angry and says he fled because he knew the LORD is gracious and slow to anger; the LORD prepares a gourd and then a worm and wind, and asks whether he should not spare Nineveh with its many people and cattle.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what the LORD teaches Jonah with the gourd in Jonah 4?","ev":["Explain why Jonah was angry (4:2)","Describe the gourd, the worm and the question in 4:10-11"],"pp":[[31,4,1,11]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_book_mat","p":1,"x":244,"y":629,"s":-2,"g":5,"bk":"MAT","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"Matthew: overview","d":"The gospel of Matthew, from the genealogy of Jesus Christ, son of David and son of Abraham (1:1), through the five great discourses, the passion and the resurrection, to the closing commission (28:16-20).","q":"Can {{name}} explain in a few sentences what Matthew is about and how it begins and ends?","ev":["Describe the movement of the book: birth and preparation (1-4), the Sermon on the Mount (5-7), miracles and mission (8-12), parables of the kingdom (13), teaching on the way to Jerusalem (14-23), the coming kingdom (24-25), the passion and resurrection (26-28)","Name where the book starts and ends"],"pp":[[39,1,1,25],[39,2,1,23],[39,3,1,17],[39,4,1,25],[39,5,1,48],[39,6,1,34],[39,7,1,29],[39,8,1,34],[39,9,1,38],[39,10,1,42],[39,11,1,30],[39,12,1,50],[39,13,1,58],[39,14,1,36],[39,15,1,39],[39,16,1,28],[39,17,1,27],[39,18,1,35],[39,19,1,30],[39,20,1,34],[39,21,1,46],[39,22,1,46],[39,23,1,39],[39,24,1,51],[39,25,1,46],[39,26,1,75],[39,27,1,66],[39,28,1,20]],"tier":"contextual"},{"id":"bt_mat_sign_of_jonah","p":1,"x":432,"y":629,"s":-2,"g":5,"bk":"MAT","ty":"THEME","t":"The sign of Jonah","d":"Asked for a sign, Jesus says only the sign of Jonah will be given, the three days in the whale, and that Nineveh and the queen of the south will condemn that generation; he adds a saying about an unclean spirit returning.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what Jesus meant by the sign of Jonah?","ev":["State the one sign Jesus promises","Explain why Nineveh and the queen of the south are mentioned"],"pp":[[39,12,38,45]],"tier":"contextual"}],"edges":[[1,0,0],[2,1,1],[3,2,1],[4,3,1]],"rel":[[2,6,2,[[31,1,17,17],[39,12,40,40]]],[3,6,2,[[31,3,5,5],[39,12,41,41]]],[0,5,2,[[31,1,17,17],[39,12,40,40]]]]}
